+// AURORA_COMPAT_WRITE_STAGING: the frame's data goes to the GPU with
+// Queue::WriteBuffer instead of through mapped staging buffers. Mapping the
+// usual StagingBufferCount buffers needs over 300 MiB of mappable memory, and
+// Firefox refuses more than about 96 MiB of it. In the browser build every
+// frame is encoded and submitted inline, so the write is ordered after the
